<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine utility to sell $100 mln bond.</title>
<headline>Argentine utility to sell $100 mln bond.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Argentina's hydroelectric power company Piedra del Aguila SA said Friday it has approved the sale of a $100 million bond under its $300 million debt program.</p>
<p>The company's directors approved the five year issue on Wednesday. This is the fifth issue sold under the debt program.</p>
<p>The bond, which has a coupon of 10.625 percent, will be sold on October 9 at a price of 99.677.</p>
<p>The first coupon payment will be made in April 1997, and subsequent payments will be quarterly.</p>
<p>-- Axel Bugge, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 3180668</p>
</text>
